# Codex PLAN review — P8B data-disco-* metadata conventions (disclaude)

See "## PR P8B" in disclaude.md. Key question is a LAYERING DEVIATION: the spec puts semantic_metadata.py in
packages/tools/src/disco/tools/appkit/, but render_html() lives in CORE (packages/core/.../appkit/models.py) and
already emits hardcoded "data-disco-section"/"data-disco-field" strings. core cannot import tools. So I propose
putting the CANONICAL vocabulary + emit + validate in core/appkit/semantic_metadata.py and refactoring the
renderer to use it (eliminating the hardcoded strings = single source of truth), with tools/frontend importing
the core module. Test in packages/core/tests/.

API: DataDiscoAttr(str,Enum) of the 8 attrs; attr(a,value)->escaped ' data-disco-x="..."'; screen_label_value
via P8A normalize_screen_label; extract_metadata(html); validate_no_duplicate_anchors; validate_anchors_not_invented.
Renderer refactored to emit via attr() + add data-disco-screen-label per section + data-disco-version on <html>.

Judge: (a) is the core-not-tools placement the RIGHT call for single-source given the layering, or is there a
reason to keep it in tools? (b) is the attr vocabulary complete/correct for P8C frontend resolution + P8D
oracles? (c) the validators — duplicate-anchor + anchor-not-invented — operating on rendered HTML, is that the
right surface, or should validation be on the AppSpec? (d) does refactoring the renderer risk changing existing
output in a way that breaks current appkit tests (byte-equivalence concerns for the lead_form starter from P7)?
(e) scope. Return APPROVE|REVISE|BLOCKED + REASONS + REQUIRED_REVISIONS.
