     1	"""Semantic reference model (P8A) — deterministic human→target resolution.
     2	
     3	A user says "the hero headline", "the second service card", "slide 5", "section 3". This
     4	resolves such a phrase to a TYPED target against a structured screen inventory
     5	(SemanticReferenceContext) — deterministically, 1-index-safe, and REJECTING ambiguity
     6	rather than guessing. The frontend (P8C) and the edit tools (P8B/P4) consume the typed
     7	targets; this module is pure (no runtime/tool imports).
     8	
     9	Invariants: a resolution is either RESOLVED (exactly one typed target) or it carries a
    10	reason (AMBIGUOUS with candidates / NO_MATCH / INVALID_ORDINAL / OUT_OF_RANGE) and resolves
    11	to nothing. It never invents a target it isn't sure about.
    12	"""
