    31	 *
    32	 * Returns `null` when the oid is empty, has no `file` part, or carries no usable
    33	 * positive line number — i.e. it is NOT a real, editable source reference. The
    34	 * caller uses `null` to gate the edit affordance off (no false affordance for a
    35	 * non-stamped / dynamically-inserted element whose oid is blank).
    36	 *
    37	 * The line is the part AFTER the last colon, so a `file` containing a colon
    38	 * (unusual but legal on some filesystems) still parses. A `:0` (the stamper's
    39	 * fallback when lxml had no source line) yields `null` — there is no real line to
    40	 * steer toward.
