     1	/**
     2	 * Selection bridge — versioned postMessage transport between host and preview iframes.
     3	 *
     4	 * Security model
     5	 * ─────────────
     6	 * Every frame carries `{v:1, channel:"disco-select", nonce}`.
     7	 *
     8	 * • srcdoc iframes (sandboxed, no allow-same-origin): the browser reports
     9	 *   `event.origin === "null"` (the string). Origin is structurally unverifiable,
    10	 *   so we accept the string "null" and rely on the per-session nonce as the sole
    11	 *   security gate.  The nonce is generated on each arm() call and sent to the
    12	 *   frame via the arm command; a forged postMessage from a co-sandboxed frame
    13	 *   would have to guess the nonce.
    14	 *
    15	 * • live-proxy iframes (allow-same-origin): `event.origin` is the preview host
    16	 *   URL. Both origin AND nonce are validated.
    17	 *
    18	 * Any frame failing validation is silently dropped.
    19	 *
    20	 * @module selectionBridge
    21	 */
    22	
    23	// ─── Public types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    24	
    25	/** A deck element reference (ref fields are schema-frozen by Track C / C4). */
